WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.160
"A Taste of Winter"

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.160
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.160
Citizens of Ikebukuro!

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:19.250
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:19.250
We are a group working to restore our country's pride.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.870
Next Saturday, here in Ikebukuro,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.500
"CRF"

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.500
we will hold a demonstration
to call attention to our work!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.870
"CRF"

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.870
I encourage all of you to take part!

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.120
Let us take back our homeland!

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.450
In other words, one of those
so-called hate rallies?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:41.000
That's right. They shout things like
"Get out of Japan, member-of-whatever-group,"

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.660
and when they find someone matching
that description, they hurl abuse at them.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.000
Fumika Jounouchi's group indiscriminately
targets Asian immigrants.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.450
--We'll be waiting for all of you
to join us next Saturday.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.580
--They call themselves Citizens for Removing
All Foreigners from Our Native Japan.
--We'll be waiting for all of you
to join us next Saturday.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.660
--Or the CRF, for short.
--Please take a stand by our side!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.660
She's not related by blood,
but I have a little sister who's Chinese.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.750
Why do we have to be bodyguards for <i>those </i>guys?

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.450
I hear you guys are a group
that's opposed to them.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:16.160
Yeah. Our Association Against
Hate Speech and Ethnic Discrimination

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.410
is critical of claims
and actions such as theirs.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.660
It's just that some amongst
our number are an extreme faction,

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.330
and they want to use force
to stop our opponents.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.790
But if that happens, we might
end up as the bad guys.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.450
So, that's why you requested me
and the G-Boys as bodyguards.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.000
It's ironic, having to protect
enemies from your own allies.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.330
As long as I receive the
standard fee, it's fine by me.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:44.620
But I really don't get it.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.910
I thought this kind of demonstration
was prohibited by law.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:53.080
And isn't it the government's policy
to promote foreign immigration?

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.540
"Ikebukuro Station"

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.540
Modern Japan would stop running if it
weren't for foreign laborers coming over.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.910
"Ikebukuro Station"

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.910
Until a few years ago,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.950
"Ikebukuro Station"

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.950
even this area was in danger
of vanishing due to population loss.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.410
What turned that around was
an influx of foreign residents.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.700
I'll bet.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.410
So, what's the point of holding
a demonstration like that now in Ikebukuro?

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.160
The laws are actually getting stricter,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.660
and such demonstrations
are hardly ever held anymore.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.250
So I don't know what they're thinking.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.450
There's something behind this.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.750
Welcome home, Mako-bro!

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.450
What's up, Guo?

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.120
Today's not the day you come help out, is it?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.370
It's not that, I brought a guest.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:14.410
A friend of mine needs to talk to you.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:15.700
Oh!

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.950
Hello!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.790
I'm Meifaa Yamashita,

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:24.700
and I run a Chinese restaurant at the
nearby Ikebukuro Paradise building.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:25.830
Go with them, Makoto.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:26.700
Huh?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.330
I'll look after the shop.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.580
You sure?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.200
Be of help to Guo-chan and this lady.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.160
We Ikebukuro shopkeepers
have to look out for one another.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.000
Thank you. It's reassuring to hear you say so.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.370
It's been 20 years since
I set up shop in this building.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.620
"Kayou Hanten | Chinese Cuisine | Lunch menu"

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.620
It's been 20 years since
I set up shop in this building.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.790
"Kayou"

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.790
My wife Meifaa is from Hunan Province, China.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.450
We met ten years ago and got married.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:01.750
The neighborhood is full of nice people,
and the restaurant is doing well.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.450
But recently...

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.290
Harassment, huh?

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.870
The same thing has happened
to other shops that employ foreigners.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.660
It's terrible, isn't it?
They haven't done anything wrong.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.040
Do you have a security camera?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.330
We do, but the people who
did it concealed their faces.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:25.250
Aren't there people active in Ikebukuro
who want to drive out foreigners?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.580
I wondered if this place is being
harassed, too, because of that.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.080
The work of those guys, huh?

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.410
Is there anything else?

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:36.750
A while back, there was a small
fire at a café in this building.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.540
The café that caught on fire
ended up shutting down.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.250
I'll try talking to that person, too.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.290
At any rate, I need info.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:50.370
"School route"

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:50.370
Sorry, Mako-bro. I know
you're busy enough already.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.660
"School route"

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.660
It's okay. Looks like it's related
to the job I'm currently doing, anyway.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.000
Meifaa and her husband are such good people.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:05.290
And yet, just because she's not from
this country, they harass and bully her.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.500
What about you? Are things going
well at your new workplace?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.700
Yeah. Everybody's nice to me.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:16.000
My father's surgery in China went well, too.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.450
It's all thanks to you and Mom.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.540
"For pedestrian and bicyclist use"

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:31.120
I have my Japanese citizenship now,
but I'm still Chinese, aren't I?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.330
That's never going to change.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.950
I can't get by anywhere but in this town,

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:42.250
so it hurts so much when
they tell me to die, or to get out.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:53.410
Ikebukuro Paradise is officially
named the Third Shouei Building.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:56.790
At the time, it was as stylish as buildings got.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.910
Apartments up top, shops down below.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:04.790
I ran the Classic Café, from the
time the building was completed.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.450
I heard there was a small fire in the café.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:10.200
Yeah, cause unknown.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.330
In the end, I decided it must have been
the amp I used in my audio setup.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.290
I see.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:20.290
Then, maybe it's unrelated
to the current incidents.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.750
Incidents?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.790
The Ikebukuro Paradise shops are being harassed.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.250
Kayou Hanten, for instance.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.450
Yamashita-san's place?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.910
You were never sure about what caused the fire?

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.950
It could be that somebody...

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.120
No, that was just an accident!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.790
Sorry, it looks like I can't help you.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:43.000
Now drink your tea, and go.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.910
"Kitakami Shinkin Bank"

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.790
Saru?

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.790
Have you heard any rumors lately
about the Ikebukuro Paradise area?

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:54.250
That building?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:58.450
Let's see, just that redevelopment
is expanding even further.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.870
Redevelopment? That's still going on?

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.620
The North Gate, this time.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.410
I heard a Chinese fund linked up
with a Japanese corporation.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:11.700
Well, it's good for us if Ikebukuro livens up.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:16.080
As long as they don't invade our turf,
I'd say they're free to have at it.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.200
"Nao"

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:31.330
It's a Beijing central government fund company
that's planning the redevelopment.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:35.040
The money is moving into Japan's Empire Realty.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.040
It's that real estate firm
that's spearheading the project.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.790
What kind of company is it?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.330
The Beijing fund has already
bought all its stock shares,

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.830
so that makes it a Chinese real estate firm.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.160
It appears to be buying up
prime metropolitan locations.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.950
Have you heard of Ikebukuro Paradise?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.910
That place is the centerpiece
of the redevelopment.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:02.790
Empire Realty wants to demolish the
current building and put up a new one.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.830
The shops there are being harassed.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.410
Do you think it's connected
with the redevelopment?

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.500
Would it be?

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:14.870
It's a group that wants to expel
foreigners that's doing the harassment.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.200
Meanwhile, a Chinese business
is spearheading the redevelopment.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.830
It's difficult to imagine there's common ground.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.620
I'll say.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.040
Then I guess the harassment and the
redevelopment are two different stories.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.540
Hisano-san?

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.540
Huh?! He got beat up?!

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.830
"Hospital"

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.830
I was handing out fliers and collecting
signatures at the East Gate.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.830
Then I was jumped on my way home.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:50.040
It's a pity you were harmed, but now
we can show the press how violent they are.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.250
I'll set up a news conference immediately.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.620
That's all you're going to do?!

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.620
One of our own got beat up!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.080
Hisano-san, I can't stick with you anymore!

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.700
We should answer violence with violence!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.790
If we do that, we'll just be
lowering ourselves to their level!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.750
If you get hit, hit back!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.370
Otherwise, they'll just look down on you!

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.200
There are plenty of others who think like me.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.620
We're going to do our own thing for a while!

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.200
Wait!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.660
So those are your group's extremists.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.540
Shouldn't you go after them?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.750
I'll try talking to them again
once they cool down.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.500
They're genuine, in their own way.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.410
The North Gate redevelopment?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.540
You think that has something
to do with this case?

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:43.870
I don't know. Some parts don't match,
and there's no single line connecting them.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:48.200
It's obvious that getting violent
will get the cops involved.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:53.000
And yet, somebody does something
that makes them the villain?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:58.750
Who the hell did it, and why?
What are they up to?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:04.620
Guo? What's up?

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:08.250
Mako-bro, there's trouble!
Ikebukuro Paradise is on fire!

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.540
Mako-bro!

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:19.910
Meifaa-san! Yamashita-san! You're not hurt?!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.700
No, we're fine. But...

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.700
Maruoka-san, on the sixth floor,
apparently passed away.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.000
What caused the fire?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:36.410
I don't know, but a police officer
said it could be arson.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:40.500
This is a declaration of war against our town.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.750
Makoto, figure out who needs crushing.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.160
Then, the G-Boys will bring them down.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.000
"Episode 9"

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.250
It's Makoto.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:56.700
Figured out anything?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.250
No, it's like the news is saying.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.120
Could be arson, could be accidental.
We're still not sure.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.620
The apartment where the fire
broke out was messy to begin with,

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.290
and there were lots of combustibles,
like books and papers.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.790
That's why it could simply be an accident.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:15.450
If it was arson, they must
have chosen it deliberately.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.330
So that a fire breaking out there
wouldn't seem suspicious.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:20.580
Okay, thanks.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.910
Hey, if you know anything, tell me!

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.000
Have you got any ideas?

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.540
I still don't know.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.500
Just make sure security is tight
for that demonstration this weekend.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:34.410
Huh? What are you getting at, Makoto?!

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:37.250
Do you think Jounouchi's group is responsible?

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:41.290
I'm not sure. The fire broke out
in a regular residence.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.410
There's no reason to target that.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:46.540
"Paradise"

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.660
"Paradise"

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.660
Ikebukuro has changed.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:54.410
The town has cleaned up, and huge
building after building goes up.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:59.620
Did you know? Ikebukuro currently ranks high
for towns where people want to live.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.370
Isn't that a good thing?

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:07.410
The old Ikebukuro had a wild anarchy
kind of image, but now that's changing.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.700
"Paradise"

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.700
But there are things I don't want to see lost.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.080
"Paradise"

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.080
The free, unassuming atmosphere.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.830
"Paradise"

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.830
The sense that, even if you're young
or poor, or you've lost everything,

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:24.410
"Paradise"

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:24.410
you can come to this town and meet
kindred spirits, and find some way to get by.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:30.160
If such things go away,
and hatred and indifference spread,

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.120
it'll make me feel sad, as someone
who grew up in this town.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:39.790
No matter how the town changes,
we'll just have to go on living here.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.330
You got that right.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.830
Makoto, what'll you do next?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.910
Talk to Jounouchi.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:50.250
I'm not wrapping my head
around this current case at all.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:54.700
I plan to keep moving around,
until something comes to light.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.580
I doubt she'll simply meet with you.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:58.950
How will you do it?

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.540
I'll suggest a meeting with Hisano.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.290
"Monthly Street Beat Writer Makoto Majima"
"Representative Toshiki Hisano"

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.290
We'd like to discuss the Saturday demonstration.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.750
"Secretary Kouzou Tsukamoto"
"Representative Fumika Jounouchi"
"Administrative Assistant Zenji Sekiya"

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.750
We'd like to discuss the Saturday demonstration.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.330
"Secretary Kouzou Tsukamoto"
"Representative Fumika Jounouchi"
"Administrative Assistant Zenji Sekiya"

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.330
Hisano-san hired our team

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.700
to secretly protect the demonstration

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.200
from an attack by extremists in his own group.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.580
It doesn't look like it'll
be that simple, though.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.120
A member of the group was attacked.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.580
As things stand, there are
sure to be some injuries.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.410
We already issued a statement.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:30.080
Whoever attacked their group,
and whoever set fire to that building,

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.700
it was not us.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:35.870
That's right! Someone's trying to set us up!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.160
Maybe <i>you </i>guys are actually
the ones orchestrating it?!

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:42.080
You don't intend to quarrel with us, correct?

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.290
We do not.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:48.580
If you attempt to end the demonstration
without violence, we will respond in kind.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.120
But if you attack, we'll fight back.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.290
We're just as fed up as you are.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:57.830
For now, I'm willing to take you at your word.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:02.500
All we want is to dispel the humiliation
this country has suffered.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.910
You should all give this plenty of thought.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:12.580
She's warped in a fascinating way,
but she's probably not guilty.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:16.540
But there's still no reason
to indiscriminately shout threats

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:20.660
at women and children
just to "dispel humiliation."

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:24.370
Acting that way only ends up
debasing yourself, in the end.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:28.580
That Tsukamoto guy wasn't
quite on the same wavelength.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:33.040
He had the scent of a front company
or some shady group.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:34.450
"Representative Fumika Jounouchi"

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:35.450
"Kouzou Tsukamoto"
"Zenji Sekiya"                         "Fumika Jounouchi"

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.200
Kouzou Tsukamoto, huh?

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.000
"Majima Produce"

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.830
Ah. Welcome home.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.580
You have another guest.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:45.950
Guest?

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:53.750
"Chinese Cuisine"
"Will open soon"

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.950
"Chinese Cuisine"
"Will open soon"

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.950
I'm sorry. I was a coward.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.620
I'm sorry. I was a coward.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.790
What's the matter, Torii-san?

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:03.330
There shouldn't be reason for you to apologize.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:07.250
I was just over at Maruoka-san's funeral.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:09.660
The entire family was in tears.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.580
If I'd only been brave enough to confess,

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.410
something like that might never have happened.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.830
"Memorandum"

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.370
This is the memorandum
Tokutomi Industries forced on me.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.620
An agreement that,
upon moving out of this building,

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.370
I'd never divulge the whole truth.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:30.200
The other residents probably didn't know this,

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.830
but the harassment from these guys was terrible.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:36.620
And so, I ran away from Ikebukuro Paradise.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:37.950
They're land sharks?

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.290
Yes.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:44.120
They harass you severely to make
you want to leave the building.

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:48.790
There are several others
besides me who left because of it.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.450
I didn't know...

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:54.540
That's because they worked
their way down from the upper floors.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.540
They probably hadn't
started in on the first floor.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:58.830
Just a minute.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:04.450
But, I thought the ones harassing us
were a group who hates foreigners.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:06.040
"I understand and accept the above matter."
"Tokutomi Industries, Inc."
"Representative Director Kouzou Tsukamoto"

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.950
There's the connection!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.870
I had a feeling something
like that had happened.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:15.830
Which means you thought
something was amiss, too.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:21.250
Tsukamoto became a sponsor
for our group not too long ago.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:27.120
We were having financial troubles,
so he seemed like he was heaven-sent.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.750
That's why he quickly became
our second-in-command.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:32.830
His influence increased,
and Representative Jounouchi

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:36.160
found she had no choice
but to listen to his opinions.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:39.450
That's also why you decided to hold
a demonstration in Ikebukuro?

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.160
Yes. To tell the truth, we, too, were wondering

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:46.950
why we should have to hold
a demonstration now in Ikebukuro.

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:48.620
And to think, it's...

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:52.000
...being used as cover for land sharking.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.950
And with Chinese funds backing it.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:59.330
Tsukamoto was trying to drive out
the Ikebukuro Paradise residents.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.080
But his guys would get busted
if they went too far.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.040
So, they schemed so that suspicion
would fall on you guys.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:10.040
We were being used, in other words.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.540
So were Hisano's people and the G-Boys.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:14.160
After all, if things get more violent,

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:18.160
Tsukamoto's people can use that
as cover to make their job easier.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.870
Torii-san said he's going to notify the police.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.200
You should cut ties with Tsukamoto right away.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.370
I'll report to our representative immediately.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.620
Tsukamoto will probably be ousted
before the night is through.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.540
However... it's too late
to call off the demonstration.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:38.580
Please, talk to the other group again
so that there's no further trouble.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.250
All right. I don't want anyone
to get hurt either.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.700
But...

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.080
But?

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.290
"Stop hurting Japan!" "Break off relations"
"Foreigners get out!"

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.540
"Stop hurting Japan!" "Break off relations"
"Foreigners get out!"

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.540
Let's take Ikebukuro back into Japanese hands!

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.410
"CRF"

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.410
Let's take Ikebukuro back into Japanese hands!

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.040
"CRF"

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.040
Take it back!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:57.200
Filthy foreigners, get out!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.000
Get out!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.580
Go back to your own countries!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.040
Go back!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:06.830
"CRF"
"Citizens for Removing All Foreigners
from Our Native Japan"

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:06.830
Remove them!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.290
"Stop your hate speech" "We are all global citizens."
"AHE"

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.290
We should live together with the world's people!

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.290
"Stop your hate speech" "We are all global citizens."
"AHE"

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.290
Together!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.330
Remove them!

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.450
Live together!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:14.200
--Drive them out!

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.290
--We're all human beings!
--Drive them out!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.410
Drive them out!

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:18.750
Live together!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.410
Drive them out!

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:23.660
Looks like Hisano managed
to keep his group unified.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:27.200
I doubt Tsukamoto will keep quiet, though.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.160
He's sure to try something.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.450
Don't worry, I've got that covered.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.700
Charge!

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.290
--He's got a blade!
--Watch out!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.870
Look out, ma'am!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.790
Take this!

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.660
Die!

00:19:58.540 --> 00:19:59.950
Shadow!

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.040
I got them to split the fee.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:06.750
Dammit!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:18.250
Let's go!

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.330
Yeah!

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.660
Arrest them!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.370
That was an easy job.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.040
Next time, offer me something
with a little more bite.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:41.500
Makoto! Was that guy connected to you?!

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:45.000
No, just a random passerby.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.750
I found out why Tsukamoto's
group grew impatient.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.750
Because the Beijing firm
was exposed for corruption.

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:57.080
The executives were arrested,
and the whole firm is a mess.

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:02.080
Seems they had to hurry and collect
on what they'd invested in Ikebukuro.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.830
So, the reason Tsukamoto attacked
at the end was that he was cornered.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.870
Cause a big disturbance
to stir up trouble for later.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:14.660
Then take advantage of the confusion
to get revenge on Jounouchi and Sekiya.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.080
Or, something like that.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:20.700
I doubt Ikebukuro Paradise
will be harmed any further.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:25.040
And I think the Yamashitas can
safely keep their restaurant open.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:29.000
That's great! Yamashita-san and
Meifaa-san will be so happy!

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:32.040
There is something that worries me, though.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.580
Tsukamoto was land sharking
on behalf of Empire Realty.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:39.160
And behind him, there was
apparently some Kansai organization.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:42.750
The same place that was
abetting Donglong, previously.

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.500
What's this about?

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:49.120
That organization has been
eyeing this town for a long time.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:53.370
They find someone in Ikebukuro who's
in a tight spot, and begin by supporting them.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:56.540
That's a foothold for expanding their influence.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:22:00.290
It's a tactic invaders
have relied upon for ages.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:05.330
Hold on. Remember the
North Gate Smoke Tower case?

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:07.790
That guy was from Kansai.

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:09.370
Could it be...

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:13.040
They've been targeting Ikebukuro all this time.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.910
And they still are now.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:16.080
Most likely.

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:19.950
<i>What's up</i>

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:23.080
<i>A world where guys with plans</i>
<i>are the first to fade away</i>

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.790
<i>The thought hit me after being out all night</i>

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:28.620
<i>A gulf forms with the respectable types</i>

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:31.750
<i>The MIC you nervously gripped</i>

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:34.370
<i>Leave it behind on the stage</i>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:37.450
<i>Unable to trust in the next move</i>

00:22:37.450 --> 00:22:40.410
<i>You get down off the stage of dreams</i>

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:43.200
<i>Fade away from the bustle of the scene</i>

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.120
<i>Do you know what becomes of him after that?</i>

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:49.250
<i>In fact, are you even prepared to know?</i>

00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:52.000
<i>Now that we're involved,</i>
<i>I want to watch you take off</i>

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.750
<i>From the runway you chose</i>

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:58.750
<i>If we happen to meet again today or tomorrow</i>

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:02.410
<i>Somewhere on this Earth</i>

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:03.870
<i>Let's have fun freestyling</i>

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:06.950
<i>Like we did that time</i>

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:09.620
<i>What's up</i>

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:11.120
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.620
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:14.000
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.500
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.370
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>

